#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Write the buildgallery design kit into this repository.

This one file carries the whole kit: 42 reference boards, the component
catalogue, the fonts they need, the tokens, the sample fixtures, the 42
UI-Pnn prompts and the standing rules. Running it writes them to
<repo root>/design/ — 101 files, about 2.4 MB.

Why a script instead of the folder: a cloud Claude Code session clones the
repository, so the kit has to be committed. Moving one file into GitHub is a
single upload; moving 101 is not.

    python3 design/build-kit.py          # write the kit
    python3 design/build-kit.py --check  # verify what is on disk, write nothing

Safe to re-run: it overwrites the kit with the same bytes and touches nothing
else. Once it has run, commit design/ and the prompts can start at UI-P00.
No dependencies beyond the standard library.
"""
